// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Math-word-problem CSD with focused final-answer span strategy.
//
// Key insights from failure analysis:
// 1. Best attempt (28.6%) used simple free generation + CloseSpanIfComplete + AdaptiveConstrainedStep
// 2. Main failures: 27/49 syntax_valid_wrong (correct structure, wrong answer content)
//    - The model writes {n} + {n} * {mult} instead of n + n * mult (braces in span)
//    - The model writes verbose reasoning inside spans
// 3. 6 examples had no span emitted at all (model reasoned without << >>)
// 4. 4 examples had malformed content (braces {} in span content)
//
// Root cause: The model generates reasoning OUTSIDE spans correctly, but when it
// opens a << >> span, it sometimes puts complex or malformed content inside.
//
// Strategy improvements over best attempt:
// A) Use SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep inside spans to discourage repeating tokens
//    from the unconstrained prefix (avoids reusing {var} patterns)
// B) Use SafeTemperatureConstrainedStep at lower temperature (0.7) to make the
//    model more confident/deterministic inside spans
// C) Keep the CloseSpanIfComplete check as the first action inside a span
// D) Add a budget safety net: if budget is very low while inside a span,
//    use CloseSpanWithinBudget to force closure
// E) Use minimal guidance focused on the output format
// F) The key insight: most failures are "syntax_valid_wrong" meaning the parser
//    accepts the span but the answer is semantically wrong. This is a model
//    quality issue, not a CSD structural issue. The best we can do is ensure:
//    - Spans are always properly closed (reduce syntax failures)
//    - Inside spans, use the most accurate constrained decoding
//
// For the 27 semantic failures: use AdaptiveConstrainedStep (proven best) but
// combine with SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep to prevent the model from copying
// template variables like {n}, {mult} literally into the span.
//
// The task parser accepts arithmetic expressions. The model should output
// clean numeric expressions. The brace failures ({n} + {n} * {mult}) suggest
// the model is inserting template variable names verbatim. RepetitionPenalty
// on the generated prefix tokens will penalize these.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
